 "escapes": [],
 "wishes": [
  "bowtie: a bar with a triangular wedge at each end (a two-armed flared cross); encoded as line + 2 tri because cross would invent flared vertical arms"
 ],
 "notes": "Bilaterally symmetric about the central stem. Three goblet-topped stems (filled inverted triangles) on a crossbar with flared tips; two C-arcs flanking, each ending in flared tips; the outer stems continue below the bar into a wide bowl that is split at the bottom, each half curling inward into a spiral; a bowtie (bar with two inward-pointing wedges) with a triangular foot on the central stem."
